# ── Secrets — never commit these ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bootstrap secret is compiled into the APK and the keystore signs it;
# either one in a public repo means anyone can impersonate your build.
server/.env
server/secrets/
# Deployment bundles carry a filled-in .env. They are built to be handed to a
# host by hand, never to be tracked — a `git add -A` will otherwise sweep the
# live JWT and bootstrap secrets straight into the history.
relay-app-upload.zip
BOOTSTRAP_SECRET.txt
dist/apk/
dist/*.zip
*.part
*.part.id
android/google-services.json
android/app/google-services.json
*.jks
*.keystore
*.jks.b64
local.properties

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
.gradle/
out/
node_modules/
server/data/
*.apk
*.aab

# ── Editors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
server/.ws_smoke_test.js

# Short-lived token handoff between the Windows credential store and the
# sandbox, written by _dumptok.ps1 and removed by _rmtok.ps1.
.gh_token
